    {
      "id": "claim_121af01f20aa4523a27e7e9f257b5c73",
      "statement": "A stored secret reads back as bullets (redaction placeholder) while one never set reads back blank. The accounts feature step performs read-modify-write with those placeholders passed straight back so the server restores the stored value for any field still holding one — diffing or stripping 'empty-looking' fields would write bullets over a real secret. New credentials are resolved at apply time via fromEnv only when the value is not already stored.",
