    {
      "id": "claim_90d282488ff8448294bdba800c91015e",
      "statement": "Nothing in the client knows which consent versions are current — the server decides what is being accepted — so publishing new terms requires no client change and no redeploy: the same build simply meets a new form on its next request. The only hand-maintained version strings are the Version lines in public/terms.html and public/privacy.html, which the setup never reads.",
