    {
      "id": "claim_a70daee640e34e1094c47ef3c224f62a",
      "statement": "The acceptance request states nothing about what is accepted: the client sends consents with no versions, and the permission's mergeRequest stamps latestConsents and $push-es onto the consents history with a server-side @now acceptedAt, so a client cannot accept terms it was never shown or backdate an acceptance. latestConsents is written as a nested object, never dotted keys, because a request setting both a field and a path inside it is refused by MongoDB with ConflictingUpdateOperators.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/ConsentsGate.tsx#L23-L41",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ac5c7d4cb275d549553aa65ffb6421ed0ecc5e88be05e461cd1d8d3c18d757d4:"
        },
